{{!
    @template theme_nadine/block_myoverview/progress-bar

    The dashboard's course progress as a measure rather than a sentence.

    Core prints "75% complete" as muted text, which reads as metadata and
    cannot be compared between cards at a glance. This renders the same value
    as a small ring beside a figure and caption. The ring carries the
    progressbar role and the core "Course progress" label; the visible figure
    and caption are hidden from assistive tech so the value is not read twice.

    The ring is deliberately the same shape as the one in the course hero, so
    a learner meets one progress language across the site.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * progress - Integer 0-100

    Example context (json):
    {
        "progress": 50
    }
}}
<div class="nl-mprogress">
    <div class="nl-mprogress__ring" role="progressbar" aria-valuenow="{{progress}}"
        aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100"
        aria-label="{{#str}}courseprogresscaption, theme_nadine{{/str}}"
        style="--nl-progress: {{progress}};">
        <span class="nl-mprogress__ring-value">{{progress}}<small>%</small></span>
    </div>
    <div class="nl-mprogress__copy" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="nl-mprogress__label">{{#str}}courseprogresscaption, theme_nadine{{/str}}</span>
    </div>
</div>
